what is completion service.
CompletionService is an interface that decouples the submission of asynchronous tasks from the processing of their results.
The concrete implementation, ExecutorCompletionService, uses an Executor to run tasks and places the results of completed tasks
into an internal queue.

Feature 	CompletableFuture	CompletionService
Purpose	To build a fluid, reactive pipeline of dependent and independent asynchronous tasks and process their results and errors.
	To process the results of a batch of submitted tasks as they complete, without needing to know which one will finish first.
Model	Offers a functional, callback-based API for handling completion and chaining tasks non-blockingly.
	Provides a queue-based model for retrieving completed tasks from a batch.
Use Case	Ideal for complex, multi-stage asynchronous workflows where you want to declaratively define a sequence of operations.
	Best for scenarios like parallelizing a task across multiple "worker" tasks and processing the results one by one as they finish.

